  "reading": "the screen is passed by a small group of middle-income regions with working institutions, no armed conflict, moderate trade openness and almost everyone better off at the base salary; most gaining regions fail on institutions or conflict, and the most open economies fail on imports. A first member therefore exists on the data, but it is not a poor region and not a rich one: it is a stable middle-income region whose people gain and whose borders are manageable. Nothing here says such a region would vote to join.",
